'<!-- Section properties of a circular sector: area, centroid, second moments of area and radii of gyration as functions of radius and central angle. -->
'<h1>Geometrical Properties of Circular Sector</h1>
'<div style="max-width:150mm"><img style="height:120pt;" alt="sector.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/sector.png"></div>
#UI 'Radius -'r = 1m
#UI 'Angle -'α = 90°
a = sqr(2*r^2*(1 - cos(α)))
'Area
A = α/2/1rad*r^2
'Centroid
y_c = a/2
z_c = 4*r*sin(α/2)/(3*α/1rad)
'Perimeter
P = (α/1rad + 2)*r
'Second moments of area
I_y = r^4*((α/1rad + sin(α))/8 - 8*sin(α/2)^2/(9*α/1rad))
I_z = r^4*(α/1rad - sin(α))/8
'Polar moment of area
I_x = I_y + I_z
'Radii of gyration
r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)
r_z = sqrt(I_z/A)
r_x = sqrt(I_x/A)
